BattleDuty #2130 verification, Windows pinned GodotJS 4.6.1 custom_build.14d19694e
Base c51312439; fix 2eb224146. All native runs headless, with owned named instances/sessions.
No full arena regeneration or deletion. No visual/player-facing changes.

Root cause: FLAG_BUNDLE_RESOURCES in Godot's binary saver collects external
resources internally, but write_variant still emits external indices from their
resource paths. A single external BoxShape3D reproduces the invalid index and null
shape without any arena cache or imported assets. Ordinary external saving works;
duplicate_deep(ALL) then compressed saving preserves it with zero dependencies.
Reference: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/4.6-stable/core/io/resource_format_binary.cpp

The large arena also exceeded the 60s generator deadline before reaching save:
328284 physics nodes, 322923 shape uses, only 13270 unique shapes. Cache each shape
signature/proxy mesh during construction and hash binary geometry. Publish the
sentinel after reload/signature/dependency verification, before temporary node cleanup.
The builder source fingerprint invalidates the old cheap cache automatically.

